# Trivy CVE exceptions for orkyo-community
#
# Format:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # Impact | Reason | Added: YYYY-MM-DD | Review: YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Policy: time-bound only. Review date must be within 14 days of added date.
# Remove entries once the upstream fix is available.
#
# 2026-10-09: foundation 1.4.0 moved the Keycloak base to 26.7.5 (community bump ce9a79f).
# A Trivy scan of quay.io/keycloak/keycloak:26.7.5 (HIGH+CRITICAL, this day) reports only
# the mssql-jdbc false positive below plus UBI9 pcre2 findings, and the container scan of
# the built orkyo-community-keycloak image on main is green. The Bouncy Castle, netty,
# FreeMarker and four Jackson entries that bridged to this release are gone.

# ── Trivy false positive ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Trivy reports fix as 12.6.5 but KC ships mssql-jdbc 13.2.1.jre11 (newer); false positive.
CVE-2025-59250  # HIGH | mssql-jdbc: improper input validation — Trivy compares the installed 13.2.1 against a fix list ending 13.2.1.jre11 and calls it older; the shipped JAR is the fixed version, false positive (re-verified 2026-10-09: Keycloak 26.7.5 still ships 13.2.1) | Added: 2026-10-09 | Review: 2026-10-23

# ── Keycloak base OS layer ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2026-09-03: the KC-26.6.x-era entries that stood in this file (jackson-databind,
# micrometer, OpenJDK, libacl, pgjdbc, six netty, a jackson-core GHSA, and the two sqlite
# FTS5 ones) are gone from the image this repo actually ships — the nightly security refresh
# rebuilt the foundation KC base out from under them. Verified against the artifact CI scans,
# ghcr.io/kymr10n/orkyo-community-keycloak:sha-b1290a37, both with CI's flags and with
# --ignore-unfixed OFF: the only findings are the mssql-jdbc false positive above and the
# entry below.


# ── nginx-alpine libexpat 2.8.4-r0 — CVE-2026-93990 (frontend) ─────────────────
# 2026-09-25: nginx:1.31-alpine still resolves to the pinned digest 1ed1b0e1… (checked
# against Docker Hub that day), which carries libexpat 2.8.4-r0; the fix is 2.8.5-r0 and
# upstream has not rebuilt. Production already runs this digest, so shipping 0.27.0 is
# not a regression. Same entry as orkyo-saas. Drop and bump the digest when upstream
# rebuilds.
CVE-2026-93990  # HIGH | libexpat 2.8.4-r0 in nginx:1.31-alpine@1ed1b0e1 (fix 2.8.5-r0) | newest upstream digest df221db8 still ships 2.8.4-r0 (scanned 2026-10-09); production already runs this digest, so shipping is not a regression | Added: 2026-10-09 | Review: 2026-10-23

# ── nginx-alpine pcre2 10.48-r0 — CVE-2026-103111 (frontend) ───────────────────
# Out-of-bounds write via a crafted regular expression. nginx only compiles the
# regexes in our own config, never user input. The newest upstream
# nginx:1.31-alpine digest (df221db8, scanned 2026-10-02) still ships 10.48-r0,
# so a pin bump does not clear it. Production already runs this digest.
CVE-2026-103111  # HIGH | pcre2 10.48-r0 in nginx:1.31-alpine@1ed1b0e1 (fix 10.49-r0) | newest upstream digest df221db8 still ships 10.48-r0 (scanned 2026-10-02); regexes come only from our own nginx config; production already runs this digest, so shipping is not a regression | Added: 2026-10-02 | Review: 2026-10-16

# ── nginx-alpine libtiff 4.7.1-r0 — CVE-2026-4775 (frontend) ───────────────────
# 2026-10-09: arbitrary code execution or denial of service via a signed integer overflow
# when decoding a TIFF. nginx serves static files and never decodes an image; libtiff is
# present only as an Alpine dependency of the image. The newest upstream nginx:1.31-alpine
# digest (df221db8, scanned 2026-10-09) still ships 4.7.1-r0, so a pin bump does not clear
# it. Production already runs this image. Same entry as orkyo-saas.
CVE-2026-4775  # HIGH | libtiff 4.7.1-r0 in nginx:1.31-alpine@1ed1b0e1 (fix 4.7.2-r0) | newest upstream digest df221db8 still ships 4.7.1-r0 (scanned 2026-10-09); nginx never decodes a TIFF; production already runs this image, so shipping is not a regression | Added: 2026-10-09 | Review: 2026-10-23
